# Hearth RT8: neutralise the BoringSSL self-tests that tear the container down.
# The vendor advertises both 32- and 64-bit ABIs, but the system image's
# conscrypt APEX self-test binaries do not run here: the 32-bit APEX test exits
# 127 (no 32-bit binary), and on this device the 64-bit APEX test
# (boringssl_self_test_apex64) also exits 127. Both services carry
# reboot_on_failure, so either one shuts the Android container down during boot
# -- which unmounts com.android.runtime (bionic libc) and leaves libhybris, the
# hwcomposer compositor and the whole Hearth session with nothing to load.
#
# This file is bind-mounted over the system image's copy, so it is the only
# thing that triggers these self-tests. Run only the plain (non-APEX) 64-bit
# test, which passes; never start either APEX self-test. The self-tests are a
# FIPS crypto self-check that nothing in the Hearth bring-up (bionic, the HALs,
# hwcomposer) depends on, so skipping the APEX ones is safe.
on init && property:ro.product.cpu.abilist64=*
    exec_start boringssl_self_test64
